            "title": "Smith Douglas Homes (SDHC) Margin Decline Challenges Bullish Narratives on Quality Earnings and Premium Valuation",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Smith Douglas Homes (SDHC) delivered a mixed set of headline results: earnings are forecast to grow at 4.69% per year going forward, below the broader US market\u2019s 16% annual pace. Revenue growth is projected at 6% annually versus a market average of 10.5%. Profit margins narrowed from 8.5% to 1.4%, leading to a steep 40.6% annualized earnings decline over the past five years. The stock now trades at a Price-To-Earnings ratio of 11.1x, which is above both the industry and peer averages...",
